the mother's day weekend always a somber  occasion for a once prominent las vegas  family  40 years ago today the body of 18 year  old jamie walker was found in a wash  near lake mead  she had been raped and murdered well it  took 35 years before a suspect could be  identified and sentenced  and a rookie reporter named george knapp  was at the scene of the murder  four decades ago and has this up  eighteen-year-old jamie walker was a  deeply religious honor student  cheerleader and high school prom queen a  third generation civil rights activist  from a prominent west las vegas family  but on may 10  1981 mother's day her crushed body was  found in the las vegas wash  after being tossed from an overpass high  above she had been kidnapped from her  home and held for ransom  before being raped and murdered the  family had been awaiting news  but not this so my whole family was in  just  a panic trying to figure out what had  happened  gala walker thornton was only eight  years old at the time but she  idolized her cousin jamie and remembers  the grief that overwhelmed the walkers  especially jamie's mother eleanor i feel  like i'm letting my daughter down if i  don't find out what happened  think about her every day yeah  every day every day this is from a 2004  interview with eleanor walker she'd  reached out to the i-team  not knowing we'd been at the murder  scene on the day the body was found  23 years earlier from the beginning the  grieving mom worked the case herself  made copious notes stayed in touch with  metro cold case detectives and lobbied  news reporters to keep  jamie's story alive in 2011 she  accompanied us to the spot where the  body was recovered the first time she'd  ever been there  it was a difficult moment for everyone  present i just know it's impossible that  somebody around  here doesn't know something from the  beginning the person at the top of  eleanor's list of suspects was former  professional boxer willie the cannon  shannon  a hulking man who lived near the walkers  and who later served prison time for  raping another young woman  metro homicide detectives had a long  list of suspects  one that included shannon and police  records show that multiple generations  of cold case detectives  made jamie's murder a high priority i  think the suspects right in that file  cold case detective dave hatch was also  contacted by eleanor walker  years after the murder she didn't know  that hatch had also been on that  overpass the day  jamie was found hatch and his successors  pursued dna  evidence multiple times by 2010  the technology had advanced enough to  confirm the involvement of willie  shannon  he was arrested in florida and sat in  the clark county jail for more than five  years awaiting trial  on the day she was scheduled to give a  deposition in the case  eleanor walker's frail body finally gave  out  she died before she could see shannon  enter an alford plea  one in which he didn't admit guilt in  2017 nevada's parole board rejected  shannon's first request to be released  a few months later he was set free  anyway and returned to his family in  florida  well we were informed i got a letter two  days after they let him out and so that  was very offensive  um and just i've struggled with this  intensely my whole life but especially  as an adult  gala is a school counselor now and has a  daughter named jamie  mother's day is not a happy time for the  walker family  they suspect some of their neighbors  knew about shannon and about two  possible accomplices  but kept quiet perhaps the final chapter  of jamie's story has yet to be  written george knapp 8 news now
 

